      <p class="post-date">Senior Managing Consultant, IBM Lab Services</p>
      <p>Sought-after to lead IBM professional services engagements to deliver sophisticated apps for enterprise clients in Insurance, Energy, Transportation, Banking, and other industries using WebSphere Portal, IBM’s low-code tooling, and open-source technologies.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Lead Developer for Pacific Life and AAA for Insurance to build two enterprise insurance apps supporting policy sales and servicing.</li>
        <li>Influenced multi-million-dollar contracts by building early prototypes and presenting solutions to stakeholders.</li>
        <li>Key presenter at IBM technical conferences on low-code tooling strategy and implementation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="post-date">Advisory Software Engineer, IBM Web Experience Factory</p>
      <p>Built and enhanced data integration features (including CMIS and Lotus Domino) for IBM's low-code developer tooling for the WebSphere Portal platform. Coordinated product localization.</p>
      <p class="post-date">Software Engineer, Lotus Workplace & WebSphere Portal</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Utilized Java profiling tools to identify improvements in memory and CPU usage for Lotus Workplace 2.0.</li>
        <li>Developed an extension for Portal Search to enable searching of Portal Document Manager data, enhancing search capabilities.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="post-date">Software Engineer, IBM Lotus Center of Competency</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Developed and maintained data collection and analysis tools to support performance engineers in testing Lotus products.</li>
        <li>Designed and implemented a performance test suite using Mercury Roadrunner, identifying key performance bottlenecks in Lotus Discovery Server prior to public release.</li>
